What is Error Handling? In how many ways can you do error handling in Node js?
==================================================================
→Error handling in Node.js is used to handle runtime issues and errors without crashing the application  during the execution of the program.
→We can handle errors using try-catch, error-first callbacks, Promise catch, async-await, Express error middleware, custom errors, and global process handlers.
Got it 👍
Below are clear, short, interview-ready examples for each error-handling method in Node.js. You can remember and explain these easily.

 Try–Catch (Synchronous / await)
—------------------------------------------------
try {  const data = JSON.parse("{invalid json}");
} catch (err) {  console.log("Error:", err.message);}
→  Used for synchronous code and async-await.

 Error-First Callbacks
—------------------------------------------------
const fs = require("fs");
fs.readFile("test.txt", (err, data) => {
  if (err) {    console.log("File error:", err);    return;  }
  console.log(data.toString());
});
→ The first parameter is always an error.


 Promise .catch()
—------------------------------------------------
function getUser() {  return Promise.reject("User not found");}
getUser()
  .then(data => console.log(data))
  .catch(err => console.log("Promise error:", err));

→ Handles Promise rejections.

 Async–Await with Try–Catch
—------------------------------------------------
async function fetchUser() {  try {
    const user = await getUser();
    console.log(user);  }
 catch (err) {    console.log("Async error:", err);  }
}
fetchUser();

→ Most commonly used in real projects.

 Express Error Middleware
—------------------------------------------------
app.get("/user", (req, res) => {
  throw new Error("User not found");
});
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.status(500).json({ message: err.message });
});

→ Centralized error handling in Express
→  Must have 4 parameters

 Custom Errors
—------------------------------------------------
class NotFoundError extends Error {
  constructor(message) {
    super(message);
    this.statusCode = 404;
  }
}
throw new NotFoundError("Product not found");

👉 Used for business logic validation.

 Global Process Handlers
—------------------------------------------------
process.on("uncaughtException", err => {
  console.log("Uncaught Exception:", err.message);
});
process.on("unhandledRejection", err => {
  console.log("Unhandled Rejection:", err);
});
